hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15896","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr; Ibn Umar heard, he said: We used to practice sharecropping and saw no harm in it, until Rafi ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it, so we left it."
"15897","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no cutting off of the hand for fruit nor for palm pith."
"15898","al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Nafi al-Kalai of the people of Basrah, he said: I passed a mosque in Madinah and prayer was established, and there was an old man who blamed the muadhdhin and said: Did you not know that my father informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command delaying this prayer? He said: I said: Who is this old man? They said: This is Abdullah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij."
"15899","Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Abayah ibn Rifaah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives. He said: Whatever sheds blood and the name of Allah is mentioned over it, eat; not the tooth and the nail. And I shall tell you: as for the tooth, it is bone, and as for the nail, it is the knives of the Abyssinians. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seized booty, and a camel fled from it. They pursued it but could not, so a man shot it with an arrow and restrained it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: These camels, or he said, this livestock, have wild ones like the wildness of beasts; whatever overcomes you, do thus with it."
"15900","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me that a man of Banu Harithah narrated to him that Rafi ibn Khadij narrated to them that they went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey. He said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, alighted for lunch, he said: Each man held the halter of his she-camel, then sent it shaking among the trees. He said: Then we sat with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And our saddles were upon our camels. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his head and saw cloaks of ours in which were threads of red wool. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do I not see this redness has overcome you? He said: So we rose quickly at the word of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until some of our camels fled. We took the cloaks and removed them from them."
"15901","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said, Sa'id narrated to us, Mujahid narrated to us, he said, Usayd the son of the brother of Rafi ibn Khadij narrated to me, he said, Rafi ibn Khadij said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to Allah and obedience to His Messenger are more beneficial to us. He said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, and if he is unable to do so, let him give it to his brother to cultivate. This is Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zubaydi, Sufyan al-Thawri and Hakkam narrated from him."
"15902","Qutayba ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Rabi'a ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Hanzala al-Zuraqi, from Rafi ibn Khadij: that people used to lease farms in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the madhayanat and what al-rabi' watered and something of straw, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked leasing farms for this and forbade it. And Rafi said: There is no harm in leasing it for dirhams and dinars."
"15903","Affan narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said, Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Abaya ibn Rifa'a, from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fever is the blast of Hell, so cool it with water."
"15904","Affan narrated to us, he said, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said, al-Hakam informed me, from Mujahid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-haql. He said: I said, what is al-haql? He said: The third and the quarter. So when Ibrahim heard that, he disliked the third and the quarter, and he saw no harm in white land taken for dirhams."
"15905","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, he said, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Qariz, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from Rafi ibn Khadij: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earning of the cupper is evil, and the dowry of the prostitute is evil, and the price of the dog is evil."
"15906","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Abaya ibn Rifa'a ibn Rafi', from Rafi ibn Khadij his grandfather, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we will meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives with us. He said: Whatever causes the blood to flow and the name of Allah is mentioned over it, eat it, except the tooth and the nail, and I shall tell you: as for the tooth, it is bone, and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) obtained spoils, and a camel from them fled, so they pursued it but could not catch it, so a man from the people shot it with an arrow and stopped it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These camels, or cattle, have wild ones like the wildness of game, so if something of them overcomes you, do with it thus. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make in the division of spoils ten sheep equal to a camel. Shu'ba said: And most of my knowledge is that I heard this phrase from Sa'id, and he made ten sheep equal to a camel, and Sufyan narrated to me from him. Muhammad said: And I heard this phrase from Sufyan."
"15907","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, he said: A boy belonging to al-Nu'man al-Ansari stole small palm trees, so he was brought to Marwan, who wanted to cut his hand. So Rafi ibn Khadij said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting for fruit nor for kathar. He said: I said to Yahya, what is al-kathar? He said: The heart of the palm."
"15908","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Usayd ibn Zuhayr the son of the brother of Rafi ibn Khadij, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: When one of us had no need of his land, he would give it for a third and a quarter and a half, stipulating three streams and the qusara and what al-rabi' watered, and living at that time was hard, and it was worked with iron and what Allah willed, and benefit was obtained from it. Then Rafi ibn Khadij came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbids you a matter that was beneficial to you, but obedience to Allah and obedience to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are more beneficial to you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbids you al-haql, and says: Whoever has no need of his land, let him grant it to his brother or let him leave it. And he forbids you al-muzabana, and al-muzabana is that a man has great wealth of palm trees, then a man comes to him and says: I have taken it for such-and-such wasqs of dates."
"15909","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Usayd ibn Zuhayr, he said: When one of us had no need of his land, then he mentioned the hadith, and he said: stipulating three streams, and al-qusara is what falls from the ear of grain."
"15910","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Mujahid narrating from Usayd ibn Zuhayr, he said: When one of us had no need of his land or needed it, he would give it for a half and a third and a quarter, stipulating three streams and the qusara and what al-rabi' watered, and we used to work in it hard work and obtain benefit from it. Then Rafi ibn Khadij came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a matter that was beneficial to you, but obedience to Allah and obedience to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are better for you. He forbade you al-haql, and said: Whoever has land, let him grant it to his brother or let him leave it. And he forbade us al-muzabana, and al-muzabana is a man having great wealth of palm trees, then a man comes and takes it for such-and-such wasqs of dates."
"15911","Yahya ibn Sa'id and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Yahya said, from Ubayd Allah, Nafi' informed me, he said: Ibn Umar used to lease farms, then it reached him that Rafi' transmits concerning it a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Ibn Umar went out to him at al-Balat and asked him, and he informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing farms. So Abd Allah abandoned leasing them. Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: So Ibn Umar went to him, and I went with him. And thus my father said."
"15912","And Muhammad ibn Ubayd also narrated it to us, he said: So Ibn Umar went, and I went with him."
"15913","Yazid narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, he said, Ibn Ajlan informed us, from Asim ibn Umar, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yazid said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Pray the morning prayer at dawn brightness, for it is greater for the reward, or for its reward."
"15914","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abaya ibn Rifa'a, from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: Jibril, or an angel, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How do you regard those who witnessed Badr among you? They said: Our best. He said: Likewise they are with us, our best among the angels."
"15915","Waki' and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cultivates land without the permission of its owners, he gets his expenses. Abu Kamil said in his hadith: And he has nothing of the crop."
"15916","Waki' narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from the son of Rafi ibn Khadij, from his father, he said: He came to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a matter that was a kindness to us, but obedience to Allah and obedience to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are kinder to us. He forbade us to cultivate land except land one of us owns its title to, or the grant of a man."
"15917","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: We used to muhaqala with land in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leasing it for a third and a quarter and specified food. Then one day a man from my uncles came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to Allah and His Messenger is more beneficial to us. He forbade us to muhaqala with land, leasing it for a third and a quarter and specified food, and he commanded the owner of the land to cultivate it or to give it to cultivate, and he disliked leasing it and anything besides that."
"15918","Isma'il narrated to us, he said, Ayyub informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: We did not see harm in sharecropping until Ibn Khadij claimed last year that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"15919","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that he said, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: O son of Khadij, what do you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning leasing land? Rafi' said: I heard my two uncles, who had both witnessed Badr, narrating to the people of the house that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing land."
"15920","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worker in charity, in truth, for the sake of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, is like the warrior in the path of Allah the Mighty and Majestic until he returns to his family."
"15921","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from Rafi ibn Khadij: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earning of the cupper is evil, and the dowry of the prostitute is evil, and the price of the dog is evil."
"15922","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"15923","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-haql. Al-Hakam said: And al-haql is the third and the quarter."
